<http://www.spektrix.com/factorytheatre/event/149202ANPGBHGNTCVJLNHDHBHTKHGQCHV> a
    schema:Event;
  schema:name "THE FAMILY CROW: A Murder Mystery";
  schema:description """
	Puppets! Puns! Muuuuuuurder!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The international hit returns to Toronto for one night only this Halloween for its 100th performance!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>A group of crows is called a murder. But what happens when there’s a murder amongst a group of crows? You get a MURDER murder mystery!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Eat your heart out, Agatha Crowstie.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Created and performed by Dora-nominated puppeteer Adam Francis Proulx and directed by Canadian Comedy Award-winner Byron Laviolette, <span class=\"ItalicText\"><span class=\"BoldText\">THE FAMILY CROW: A Murder Mystery</span></span> is a puppet-fuelled, pun-filled comic whodunit for grown-ups. One performer brings six characters to life in a delightfully spooky evening for anyone who loves a good story, a good pun, and a good twist.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Gather your flock and join us for this milestone performance!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>______.______<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Duration: approx. 70 minutes<span><br/></span>Age Recommendation: 14+<span><br/></span>Content & Sensory Warnings: Cartoonish violence, haze, loud noises, flashing lights.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>______.______
<span><br/></span>“★★★★★”<span><br/></span>- Saskatoon StarPhoenix<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>“Flock to Adam Francis Proulx’s delightfully atmospheric The Family Crow.”<span><br/></span>- Glenn Sumi, NOW Magazine<span><br/></span><span><br/></span> \"A ghoulish, screwball delight from start to finish.\"<span><br/></span>-Istvan Dugalin, Toronto<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-10-31T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
